# __NAME__

An agent scaffolded by `bide init -agent`. It handles a customer's email and can refund an order, and
it shows the one control that matters when an agent reads text it does not control: **once a model turn
has been shown untrusted content, every side effect a later turn asks for needs a human decision.** (A
side effect asked for in the same turn as the read was decided before the read returned, so it is not
held back by it: the model can ask for both at once. Read the limits below.)

```sh
go mod tidy
go run .
```

It runs with no API key and no network (the model is scripted). You will see it read the email,
pause before the refund, record the decisions of the escalation gate, refund once, and write
`declarations.json`. Run it again: nothing runs twice.

## What is in it

- `read_email` returns text from outside the program. It declares `agent.Untrusted("inbound-email")`, so
  every result it returns is recorded with that source.
- `refund` is a side effect. It has no gate of its own. It declares `agent.Trusted("the host's own refund provider")`: its results are the host's, not outside text, and the declaration says so.
- The agent has `agent.WithTaintPolicy(agent.TaintPolicy{Gate: ..., RequireProvenance: true})`. `RequireProvenance` (experimental) makes a tool with neither `Untrusted` nor `Trusted`, and a run with neither `WithUntrustedInput` nor `WithTrustedInput`, an error, so nothing is unclassified by omission. After a model turn has been shown
  untrusted content, a side-effecting call requested by a *later* turn needs the escalation gate, whatever
  the email said. The gate is a second approval on the call, under the subject `<call>#taint`, decided by
  its own approvers; an approval clears nothing, so the next side effect is asked again.
__GATE_TEXT__
- The run states where its input came from: `agent.WithTrustedInput("the operator's instruction")`. The
  customer's email is not the input; it arrives through the tool, which is marked.

## What it does not do

It bounds what a hostile email can make the agent do. It does not detect or prevent the injection: a tool
you did not mark, an approver who is persuaded, and a `ReadOnly` tool that can reach an attacker's server
are all outside it. Read the
[untrusted content guide](https://github.com/bide-ai/bide/blob/main/docs/guides/untrusted-content.md) before
you rely on it.

## Review the declarations

`declarations.json` lists the policy and every tool with what it declares. Commit it next to your code, then:

```sh
bide doctor -declarations declarations.json          # what to look at
bide doctor -diff main.json declarations.json        # exits 1 if anything is weakened
```

A removed `Untrusted`, a new `agent.TaintExempt`, a lower `need` or a requester no longer excluded is
reported as weakened.

